# A -D define a build is given reaches an enum body's `{% if %}` in the declarations pass. The gate
# dumps this file with and without -Dsemdecl_probe: the port must match the oracle each time, and the two
# oracle dumps must differ, or the fixture proves nothing. Only this site is observable through the
# hosted dump: the declarations a macro expansion writes are located in the expansion, so the oracle
# does not print them, and the inline and macro-call sites cannot be told apart by it.
enum DefineMode
  {% if flag?(:semdecl_probe) %}
    On = 1
  {% else %}
    Off = 0
  {% end %}
end
